bly, the first differences form an arithmetic progression: 4, 6, 8, 10. Given that the second difference is constant at 2, the general term simplifies to a quadratic equation: a_n = n^2 + n.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"annotations":[],"logprobs":[],"text":"The terms are the “pronic” (or oblong) numbers, i.e. products of two consecutive integers:\n\n   1·2 = 2, 2·3 = 6, 3·4 = 12, 4·5 = 20, 5·6 = 30, …\n\nHence if you start counting at n=1 the nth term is\n\n   aₙ = n·(n + 1)\n\nor equivalently\n\n   aₙ = n² + n.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_0cdcf22d3808a85f006a95bbf0c93087d0a6bcf30b13f4e166","role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message"},{"content":"Using the pattern you discovered, what would be the 10th term? And can you find the sum of the first 10 terms?","role":"user"}],"is_root":false,"log_id":"g","metadata":{"braintrust.parent":"project_name:java-unit-test","model":"o4-mini","provider":"openai","reasoning":{"effort":"high","summary":"detailed"},"request_base_uri":"http://localhost:52408","request_method":"POST","request_path":"responses","response_id":"resp_0cdcf22d3808a85f006a95bbf5a6a087d097d20e5b654a6593","x-request-id":"req_2543d397adc14b24978a0324f8def161"},"metrics":{"completion_reasoning_tokens":576,"completion_tokens":771,"end":1788197885.3264241,"estimated_cost":0.0035970000000000004,"prompt_cached_tokens":0,"prompt_tokens":186,"start":1788197877.225431,"tokens":957},"org_id":"5abfae3a-7aa7-4653-a9c8-b3efcb18f584","origin":null,"output":[{"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqlbv9129WPcKdg8d4KHpuU8fKWbJMTbz1g-IhN9CUOkZ9mlzjnLW04tfeqBpT_pd97nAuuyfQshIhku7ePFI1ySjpRhqRIM3OZYg_4RFM9J6jkWgP3Exe_hYG0a_OSE5dxOuGo8bfhMfAXk-JI2-ftngXA1hEExwEFeFbYw3JKJAo5hO30dqcGkud5EGwZChRmOR03rOfMU2kphLA2b96iUjtGta0rWgJHBleITHnWfCixTJ36BeTrGQaIotdM09IS4y4hFiGA9y7tadY9b-KzwZKkjcWwCozRKO-OzQ8nz1eZUcpwB8RCXK5b4XBt7h-rkkoFnLnTfk8XzbtDZaleFnHQGE1034XxDlJqZnqxXhejGKu4k72_rWCl656fhpHdfOytB1vzm6bKCsZDzM3vDH1r-iNyHr7a_5M8y7O26SzocHRx